@page "/discord"
@inject DiscordPresenceCache Presence

<PageTitle>Discord | ksamods.gg</PageTitle>

@*
    The page behind the Discord mark in the header.

    It exists instead of pointing that mark straight at an invite. A header icon that throws you
    out to a third-party join screen with no idea what you are joining is the kind of link people
    learn not to press. This says what the server is, whose it is, and what is in it, and then
    offers the invite.
*@

<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="shrink-0 text-muted-foreground" aria-hidden="true">
            <ProviderMark Provider="discord" Class="size-9" />
        </span>
        <div>
            <h1 class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">@Community.DiscordName</h1>
        </div>
    </div>

    @*
        Counts before the pitch, because they are the question somebody weighing a Discord invite
        actually has. Both numbers or neither: "online" without "members" reads as the whole server.
    *@
    @if (_presence is not null)
    {
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-3 rounded-lg border border-border bg-card/40 px-5 py-4">
            <div>
                <p class="tabular text-2xl font-semibold leading-none">@_presence.Total.ToString("N0")</p>
                <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-muted-foreground">members</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <p class="tabular text-2xl font-semibold leading-none text-severity-ok">@_presence.Online.ToString("N0")</p>
                <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-muted-foreground">online now</p>
            </div>

            @if (_presence.UpdatedAt is { } stamped)
            {
                @* Said plainly, because a live-looking number with no age on it is a claim we
                   cannot keep. The counter refreshes on its own schedule and we cache on top of
                   that, so this is the only honest way to show it. *@
                <p class="ml-auto font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                    counted @Presentation.Ago(stamped)
                </p>
            }
        </div>
    }

    <p class="mt-6 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        We run a Discord for KSA modding, and this site grew out of it. It has been going since
        the game came out. There are channels for releases, for work in progress, and for the
        times a mod won't load and you want somebody to look at it with you.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6">
        <Button Href="@Community.Discord" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <ProviderMark Provider="discord" Class="size-[1.05rem]" />
            Join the Discord
        </Button>
    </div>

    @*
        The disclaimer that made this page worth building. "KSA Modding Society" and "Kitten Space
        Agency" are close enough that somebody skimming will assume the invite is the game's own,
        and finding out after joining is a bad way to find out.
    *@
    <Alert Variant="info" Title="This isn't the official KSA server" Class="mt-8">
        It is the modding community's, and we run it. RocketWerkz make Kitten Space Agency and
        have nothing to do with this one. If you want theirs, it isn't ours to link to.
    </Alert>

    <section class="mt-10 border-t border-border pt-8">
        <h2 class="field-label text-muted-foreground">What you'd use it for</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
            <li>
                <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Something won't load.</span>
                A log and a description usually gets an answer, and often from whoever wrote the
                mod. This site can tell you an archive is packaged wrong, but it can't tell you
                why your install is unhappy.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="font-medium text-foreground">You're making one.</span>
                Work in progress gets posted there long before it becomes a release, which is also
                where you'll find people willing to test it.
            </li>
            <li>
                <span class="font-medium text-foreground">You want to know what's new.</span>
                Releases get announced there as they land, with the context a catalogue entry
                doesn't carry.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Something wrong with this site rather than with a mod?
        <a href="/bug" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">Report a bug</a>
        instead. It reaches the same people and doesn't get lost in a channel.
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    private DiscordPresence? _presence;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Cached and short-timeout, so this cannot hold the page up for long. Null just means the
        // counts sit this render out.
        _presence = await Presence.CurrentAsync();
    }
}
